# {{.ExportedName}} — Agent Guide

`{{.Name}}` is a go-sicky service generated by `sicky new --type standard`. It
compiles and runs without any external service{{if .Models}} once the PostgreSQL
DSN in `config.json` points at a reachable database{{end}}; `config.json`
describes its runtime configuration.

## Commands

```bash
make build   # runs `go mod tidy`, then compiles ./bin/svc
make test    # runs `go mod tidy`, then go test ./...
make docker  # builds the image; `make push` pushes it
```

The first `make build` resolves dependencies over the network. Scaffolding
itself never does.

Run the binary directly:

```bash
./bin/svc
{{if .Models}}./bin/svc --initdb   # create the database tables and exit
{{end}}```

{{if or .WithFiber .WithHTTP}}HTTP endpoints answer `/ping`:
{{if .WithHTTP}}- net/http (bunrouter) on `:9980`
{{end}}{{if .WithFiber}}- Fiber on `:3000`
{{end}}{{end}}{{if .WithGRPC}}- gRPC on `:44945`
{{end}}- Manager on `127.0.0.1:8888` (loopback by default): `/metrics`, `/health`, `/ready`, `/live`

## Configuration

- `config.go` owns the root `ConfigDef`: the `server`, `service`, `sicky` and
  `app` blocks decoded from `config.json`.
- `app/config.go` owns the application settings (`AdminUsername`,
  `AdminPassword`, `GeneralToken`), `Ensure()` and the package-level
  `app.Config` assigned in `main`.
{{if .WithAuth}}- `app/session.go` owns the in-memory access-token sessions read by
  `validateSession`.

### Credentials

The `app` block ships empty credentials. `service.Auth.Authenticate` fails
closed when either admin field is empty, so `POST /auth/login` returns 401
until both are configured. There is no default `admin/admin`, and no token is
generated at build time. Keep real values out of version control.

{{end}}{{if .Models}}### Models and the Database

`--model` is the only switch that enables bun. `config.json` ships a
placeholder DSN:

```json
"driver": "postgres",
"dsn": "postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/{{.Name}}?sslmode=disable"
```

Replace it with the real connection before starting the service. `--initdb`
(note the double dash) runs `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "uuid-ossp"`, then
every model's `InitDB`, and exits without serving.

Models use the standard library `uuid` package and declare
`bun:"id,pk,default:uuid_generate_v4()"`. That default comes from PostgreSQL's
`uuid-ossp` extension: a non-PostgreSQL driver must remove
`default:uuid_generate_v4()` from the `ID` field. `Create` assigns an ID in Go
when it is nil, so only the DDL default changes.

{{end}}## Conventions

{{if .WithHTTP}}- HTTP handler types are `HTTP<Resource>` / `NewHTTP<Resource>`, and `Name()`
  returns `"<resource>.http"`. DTOs are `Http<Resource><Method><Action>`
  (for example `HttpKeyPostCreate`).
- Handler errors leave through `utils.WrapHTTPResponse` and
  `utils.BunAutoFormat` / `utils.BunAutoFormatWithStatus`; codes and messages
  live in `handler/response` (`response.Code*`, `response.Msg*`).
{{end}}- One resource is one set of files: `model/<name>.go`, `service/<name>.go`,
  `handler/<name>.http.go`, plus declarations appended to
  `handler/request/http.go` and `handler/response/http.go`.
- Check every error; generated code contains no bare `_ =`.
- Log messages are lowercase (`logger.Logger.*Context`); error details stay in
  the server log, not in the response body.
- Use `context.Background()` or a propagated context; never `context.TODO()`.

## Adding a Resource

```bash
sicky generate model <name>
```

This writes the model, service, HTTP handler and DTO declarations, and wires
`config.json` (`sicky.infra.bun`), `main.go` (`MustInfra`, `--initdb`, `InitDB`
and the handler registration). Use `--no-wire` to write files only, and
`--force` to overwrite an existing resource; without `--force` a name that
already exists fails before anything is written.

## Tests

There is no CI configuration in this project; run `make test` (or
`go test ./...`) before committing. Generated CRUD handlers start as TODOs:
add tests alongside the behavior you fill in.
